<article class="env-definition" id="01EF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01EF">Definition <span data-tag="01EF">20.9.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $\mathcal{U} : U = \bigcup _{i \in I} U_ i$ be an open covering. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an abelian presheaf on $X$. The complex $\check{\mathcal{C}}^\bullet (\mathcal{U}, \mathcal{F})$ is the <em>Čech complex</em> associated to $\mathcal{F}$ and the open covering $\mathcal{U}$. Its cohomology groups $H^ i(\check{\mathcal{C}}^\bullet (\mathcal{U}, \mathcal{F}))$ are called the <em>Čech cohomology groups</em> associated to $\mathcal{F}$ and the covering $\mathcal{U}$. They are denoted $\check H^ i(\mathcal{U}, \mathcal{F})$. </p>
</article>